{# Runnable landing slot 'similarity_search' (§15.2): a real mmsearch example
   over the bioseq columnar (USING bioseq) fixture. Its hidden setup runs an
   EXPLAIN (FORMAT JSON) assertion that the plan is the BioseqScan custom scan,
   so a planner regression cannot silently publish the always-true stub result.
   Renders only the visible SQL and the executed result rows; hidden
   setup/teardown SQL never reaches the site. Context:
   examples.similarity_search.visible_sql and examples.similarity_search.result,
   whose result.columns each carry a name and whose result.rows are lists of
   cells with is_null and text. #}
<figure class="sql-example" id="example-similarity-search">
  <figcaption class="sql-example-title">Search sequences with <code>mmsearch</code></figcaption>
  <p class="sql-example-lede">One predicate in the WHERE clause activates the BioseqScan custom scan and returns the rows whose sequence matches the probe.</p>
  <div class="code-card">
    <div class="code-card-head">
      <span class="code-dot code-dot-a" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="code-dot code-dot-b" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="code-dot code-dot-c" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="code-card-name">query.sql</span>
      <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="sql-similarity-search" aria-label="Copy the similarity search query">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre class="code-block"><code class="language-sql" id="sql-similarity-search">{{ examples.similarity_search.visible_sql }}</code></pre>
    {% if examples.similarity_search.result %}
    <div class="result-panel">
      <table class="result-table">
        <caption>Executed query result</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
          {% for col in examples.similarity_search.result.columns %}
            <th scope="col">{{ col.name }}</th>
          {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for row in examples.similarity_search.result.rows %}
          <tr>
          {% for cell in row %}
            <td>{% if cell.is_null %}<span class="cell-null">NULL</span>{% else %}{{ cell.text }}{% endif %}</td>
          {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</figure>
